Tark: Settings > Privacy says what Tark connects to (spec 5.3).

An expandable "What Tark connects to" row lists every service the browser
itself contacts, with its hosts, in plain words. The hosts live in a new
file, tark_contacted_hosts.cc, because domain substitution rewrites Google
hosts in Chromium's string files; utils/allowed_hosts.txt mirrors them for
the network check, and a unit test keeps the two in step. The Security row's
description no longer promises Safe Browsing, which Tark does not build.

